.0"},"bio":null},"Q18388296":{"id":"Q18388296","name":"V","ko":"뷔","birthName":"Kim Tae-hyung","birthNameEn":"Kim Tae-hyung","aliases":["Taehyung","Kim Taehyung","Kim Tae-hyung"],"birth":"1995-12-30","death":"","birthplace":"Daegu","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":179,"occupations":["singer-songwriter","television actor","record producer","dancer","model","singer"],"debut":"2013","agencies":[{"name":"Big Hit Music","korean":true,"id":"Q106296918","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Hybe","korean":true,"id":"Q16161254","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q13580495","name":"BTS","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/thv/","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3JsHnjpbhX4SnySpvpa9DK","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/83096042-3785-481e-8843-dee69f1aad12"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kim Tae-hyung, known professionally as V (뷔), is a South Korean singer. In 2013, he made his debut as a member of the South Korean boy band BTS, under Big Hit Entertainment. V has performed three solo songs under BTS's name—\"Stigma\" in 2016, \"Singularity\" in 2018, and \"Inner Child\" in 2020—all of which charted on South Korea's Gaon Digital Chart. Outside of his music projects with BTS, V had his acting debut in the 2016 television series Hwarang: The Poet Warrior Youth and, with Jin, contributed the single \"It's Definitely You\" to its soundtrack. He released his first independent song, the self-composed \"Scenery\", in 2019.","title":"V (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/V_%28singer%29"}},"Q18648456":{"id":"Q18648456","name":"Lee Haena","ko":"이해나","birthName":"이해나","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lee Hae-na","Haena"],"birth":"1991-06-02","death":"","birthplace":"Incheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","stage actor"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q24856232","name":"Matilda","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/vivan.lee.925/","x":"https://x.com/A2haena","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCwM-b-hCvOqfs-55NNuHI1g","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/91b7812d-5251-4fce-960f-5521457ab223"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Lee Hae-na, credited and stylized simply as Haena, is a South Korean singer. She debuted as a member of the girl group Kiss&Cry, who released their first single, \"Domino Game\", in January 2014. Following the group's disbandment, she debuted for a second time in March 2016 as the leader of the girl group Matilda.","title":"Lee Hae-na","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lee_Hae-na"}},"Q19603912":{"id":"Q19603912","name":"Hwasa","ko":"화사","birthName":"안혜진","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Ahn Hye-jin"],"birth":"1995-07-23","death":"","birthplace":"Jeonju","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":160,"occupations":["singer","recording artist","singer-songwriter","dancer","performing artist","composer"],"debut":"2014","agencies":[{"name":"P Nation","korean":true,"id":"Q61410007","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Rainbow Bridge World","korean":true,"id":"Q16174772","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q98754857","name":"Refund Sisters","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"website":"https://pnation.com/artists/14","instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/_mariahwasa/","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCiM8arBZ-GyuBFG3wy6fEgw","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2x328mPRm6fc1nkqEvyrFF","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/9c750319-8267-493a-aaaf-305e1c6bcc21"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Ahn Hye-jin, known professionally by her stage name Hwasa (화사; sometimes stylized as Hwa Sa), is a South Korean singer, songwriter, and television personality. She rose to prominence as a member of the girl group Mamamoo in 2014. In February 2019, she made her solo debut with the song \"Twit\" which topped the Circle Digital Chart and won a Gaon Chart Music Award. In 2020, Hwasa debuted as part of the Refund Sisters with the single \"Don't Touch Me\", which reached number one in South Korea.","title":"Hwasa","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hwasa"}},"Q21824968":{"id":"Q21824968","name":"Choi Seung-cheol","ko":"에스쿱스","birthName":"최승철","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Seungcheol","S.Coups"],"birth":"1995-08-08","death":"","birthplace":"Daegu","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","rapper","dancer"],"debut":"2015","agencies":[{"name":"Pledis Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q45282","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Hybe","korean":true,"id":"Q16161254","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q14524548","name":"Seventeen","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/sound_of_coups/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/285c41b3-6a5d-48c7-8cd5-a25427765747"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Choi Seung-cheol, known by his stage name S.Coups (에스쿱스), is a South Korean rapper, singer, and songwriter. Managed by Pledis Entertainment, he is the leader of the South Korean boy band Seventeen and its hip hop team, and in 2025 debuted in a sub-unit with Mingyu as CxM.","title":"S.Coups","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S.Coups"}},"Q24276424":{"id":"Q24276424","name":"Jin","ko":"진","birthName":"김석진","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kim Seok-jin","Kim Seokjin"],"birth":"1992-12-04","death":"","birthplace":"Gwacheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":179,"occupations":["singer","songwriter"],"debut":"2013","agencies":[{"name":"Big Hit Music","korean":true,"id":"Q106296918","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q13580495","name":"BTS","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"website":"https://ibighit.com/bts/eng/discography/jin/","instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/jin/","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5vV3bFXnN6D6N3Nj4xRvaV","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/09720eec-3871-49d5-932d-eb7542768cd3"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kim Seok-jin, known professionally as Jin, is a South Korean singer. He rose to prominence as member of the South Korean boy band BTS. Jin has released three solo tracks with BTS: \"Awake\" in 2016, \"Epiphany\" in 2018, and \"Moon\" in 2020, all of which have charted on South Korea's Gaon Digital Chart. In 2019, Jin released his first independent song, the digital track \"Tonight\". He made his official debut as a solo artist in October 2022, with the release of the single \"The Astronaut\". Apart from singing, Jin appeared as a host on multiple South Korean music programs from 2016 to 2018.","title":"Jin (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jin_%28singer%29"}},"Q24566664":{"id":"Q24566664","name":"Yoon Jeong-han","ko":"정한","birthName":"윤정한","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Jeonghan"],"birth":"1995-10-04","death":"","birthplace":"Gangbuk District","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2015","agencies":[{"name":"Pledis Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q45282","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Hybe","korean":true,"id":"Q16161254","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q14524548","name":"Seventeen","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/jeonghaniyoo_n/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/84909af0-38ac-440d-bcea-496845b78a99"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fd/Jeonghan_Follow_240330.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jeonghan_Follow_240330.jpg","author":"Seventeen","license":"CC BY 3.0"},"bio":{"text":"Yoon Jeong-han, known mononymously as Jeonghan, is a South Korean singer. Managed by Pledis Entertainment, he is a member of the South Korean boy band Seventeen, its vocal team, and its subunits JxW and JxJ.","title":"Jeonghan","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeonghan"}},"Q27658440":{"id":"Q27658440","name":"Lee Na-eun","ko":"이나은","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lee Naeun","Naeun"],"birth":"1999-05-05","death":"","birthplace":"Cheongju","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor"],"debut":"2015","agencies":[{"name":"DSP Media","korean":true,"id":"Q489428","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q20858387","name":"April","start":"2015","end":"2022"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/betterlee_0824/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/4c32d23b-3c5e-45ae-8bb9-de85e203fde6"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Lee Na-eun, also known mononymously as Naeun, is a South Korean actress, model and singer. She is a former member of the South Korean girl group April, formed by DSP Media in 2015. She is best known for her roles in television series A-Teen (2018), A-Teen 2 (2019) and Extraordinary You (2019).","title":"Lee Na-eun","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lee_Na-eun"}},"Q28653640":{"id":"Q28653640","name":"Moon Tae-il","ko":"태일 (가수)","birthName":"문태일","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Taeil"],"birth":"1994-06-14","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"SM Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483938","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Avex Trax","korean":false,"id":"Q1988428","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q23725822","name":"NCT","start":"2016","end":"2024"},{"id":"Q67972645","name":"NCT U","start":"2016","end":"2024"},{"id":"Q55624444","name":"NCT 127","start":"2016","end":"2024"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/mo.on_air/","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1z0Hi3myYw4x32xCq0H3aq","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/09696205-d071-497e-86d8-774114ad6f08"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Moon Tae-il, known mononymously as Taeil, is a South Korean former singer. He was a member of the South Korean boy band NCT from 2016 until 2024, when Korean investigators tied him to a criminal sexual offense. After being accepted as a trainee by SM Entertainment in 2013, Taeil was introduced as a member of the company's pre-debut training team, SM Rookies. He later made his official debut as a singer in NCT's first sub-unit NCT U and as the lead vocalist of its Korean-based sub-unit NCT 127, in 2016. A standout and popular member of the group, Taeil broke the Guinness World Record for \"Fastest time to reach 1 million followers on Instagram\" after starting his account on July 6, 2021.","title":"Taeil (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taeil_%28singer%29"}},"Q28698248":{"id":"Q28698248","name":"Sunyoul","ko":"선율","birthName":"선예인","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Seon Yein"],"birth":"1996-11-06","death":"","birthplace":"Wando County","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q21012399","name":"Up10tion","start":"","end":""}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q30944712":{"id":"Q30944712","name":"Kim Yu-jeong","ko":"유정","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Yujeong","Kim Yujeong"],"birth":"1992-02-14","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q18344661","name":"Laboum","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/yudong_0214/","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCGOnllE3_mj5KiH5gHX6HLQ"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q31177864":{"id":"Q31177864","name":"Im So-young","ko":"소영","birthName":"임소영","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Soyoung"],"birth":"1993-09-09","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q12603717","name":"Stellar","start":"2017","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/soyoungyim/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/219b8dab-ab50-439f-a929-977df967f36b"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q47973704":{"id":"Q47973704","name":"Son Yu-ji","ko":"손유지","birthName":"손유지","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Yuji"],"birth":"1998-11-25","death":"","birthplace":"South Korea","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q55731710","name":"Apple.B","start":"","end":""},{"id":"Q65269682","name":"3YE","start":"","end":""}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q484040":{"id":"Q484040","name":"Shin Ji","ko":"신지","birthName":"Lee Ji-seon","birthNameEn":"Lee Ji-seon","aliases":[],"birth":"1981-11-18","death":"","birthplace":"Incheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","songwriter"],"debut":"1998","agencies":[{"name":"Trifecta Entertainment & Media","korean":false,"id":"Q16958129","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q487219","name":"Koyote","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/shinji_jidaeng/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/3e18e6a6-4287-4135-8865-672e1c86bc2f"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Lee Ji-seon, known professionally as Shin Ji, is a South Korean singer, lyricist and actress. She attended Dongduk Women's University – Department of Popular Music. She made her debut in 1998 in the group, Koyote, and wrote lyrics for some of the group's songs including \"I Love Rock & Roll\". She is the only female and original member of the group.","title":"Shin Ji","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shin_Ji"}},"Q486536":{"id":"Q486536","name":"Oh Yeon-seo","ko":"오연서","birthName":"오햇님","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Oh Haet-nim","Oh Yeon Seo","Oh Yeonseo"],"birth":"1987-06-22","death":"","birthplace":"Jinju","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":170,"occupations":["singer","actor","model","television actor","film actor"],"debut":"2002","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q6460281","name":"LUV","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/ohvely22/"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Oh Haet-nim, known professionally as Oh Yeon-seo, is a South Korean actress and former singer. She is a former member of the musical group Luv, and as an actress she is best known for her roles in television dramas My Husband Got a Family (2012), Jang Bo-ri is Here! (2014), Shine or Go Crazy (2015), Come Back Mister (2016), My Sassy Girl (2017), A Korean Odyssey (2017–2018), Love with Flaws (2019–2020), Mad for Each Other (2021), and Café Minamdang (2022).","title":"Oh Yeon-seo","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oh_Yeon-seo"}},"Q487560":{"id":"Q487560","name":"Sung Yu-ri","ko":"성유리","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1981-03-03","death":"","birthplace":"Tübingen","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["actor","singer"],"debut":"1998","agencies":[{"name":"DSP Media","korean":true,"id":"Q489428","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q484082","name":"Fin.K.L","start":"1998","end":"2005"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/sung_yuri_/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/07cfe635-5068-4541-9cff-cda37d5ea9a9"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Sung Yu-ri is a South Korean actress and singer. She made her entertainment debut in 1998 as a member of the K-pop group Fin.K.L. Sung turned to acting in 2002, starring in television dramas such as Thousand Years of Love (2003), The Snow Queen (2006), Hong Gil-dong (2008), and Feast of the Gods (2010).","title":"Sung Yu-ri","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sung_Yu-ri"}},"Q490056":{"id":"Q490056","name":"Ock Joo-hyun","ko":"옥주현","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Ock Ju-hyun","Ok Ju-hyeon","Ok Chuhyŏn","Ok Chuhyon","Oak Joo-hyun"],"birth":"1980-03-20","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor"],"debut":"1998","agencies":[{"name":"Stone Music Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483971","start":"","end":""},{"name":"DSP Media","korean":true,"id":"Q489428","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q484082","name":"Fin.K.L","start":"1998","end":"2005"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/o._.julia/","x":"https://x.com/joohyunieee","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2hWmACtSYPgJPolTUMKHAP","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/30bafc6a-a9d9-4c7d-b781-717bc2e5fed0"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Ock Joo-hyun is a South Korean singer and musical theatre actress, known mostly for her role as the lead singer of the South Korean girl group Fin.K.L. After their unofficial breakup in 2002, Ock released three solo albums and has participated in several musicals, namely Wicked, Aida, Chicago, Cats, 42nd Street, and The Count of Monte Cristo.","title":"Ock Joo-hyun","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ock_Joo-hyun"}},"Q56441288":{"id":"Q56441288","name":"Chaeyeon","ko":"이채연","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lee Chae-yeon"],"birth":"2000-01-11","death":"","birthplace":"Yongin","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2018","agencies":[{"name":"WM Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q19794482","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Off The Record Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q106910250","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q56402353","name":"Iz*One","start":"2018","end":"2021"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/chaestival_/","x":"https://x.com/official_LCY","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCVVFt4q2WczlzhOr4V2kYxA","tiktok":"https://www.tiktok.com/@official.lcy","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/cc79fbc1-bc7e-415e-a0ab-949b281550e7"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Lee Chae-yeon is a South Korean singer, dancer, and actress. She was a member of the South Korean-Japanese girl group Iz*One, and made her solo debut in 2022 with her first extended play (EP), Hush Rush.","title":"Lee Chae-yeon","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lee_Chae-yeon"}},"Q56506824":{"id":"Q56506824","name":"Kang Hye-won","ko":"강혜원","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Hyewon"],"birth":"1999-07-05","death":"","birthplace":"Yangsan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2018","agencies":[{"name":"8D Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q65272598","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Off The Record Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q106910250","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q56402353","name":"Iz*One","start":"2018","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/hyemhyemu/","x":"https://x.com/hyemu_official","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCGsmowjz7ctm9jiKbnmF8EA","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/fd647d11-51ea-4755-8888-cf79304ed6e1"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kang Hye-won is a South Korean actress and former singer. She was a member of the South Korean–Japanese girl group Iz*One from 2018 to 2021. As an actress, she has starred in works including Boyhood (2023) and Friendly Rivalry (2025).","title":"Kang Hye-won","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kang_Hye-won"}},"Q60566856":{"id":"Q60566856","name":"Huh Jiwon","ko":"허지원","birthName":"허지원","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Ji Won","Heo Ji-won","Huh Ji-won"],"birth":"2000-09-04","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor"],"debut":"2019","agencies":[{"name":"FNC Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q12581039","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q59325270","name":"Cherry Bullet","start":"2019","end":"2024"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/jiwxoxni/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/f1a2ca1e-47d3-4d69-9547-727471bfab90"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/ba/190604_%EC%B2%B4%EB%A6%AC%EB%B8%94%EB%A0%9B_%EC%A7%80%EC%9B%90_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:190604_%EC%B2%B4%EB%A6%AC%EB%B8%94%EB%A0%9B_%EC%A7%80%EC%9B%90_(2).jpg","author":"NINE STARS","license":"CC BY 3.0"},"bio":{"text":"Huh Ji-won, known mononymously as Jiwon, is a South Korean model, actress and singer. She is a former member of the South Korean girl group Cherry Bullet, and made her solo debut on August 5, 2026, with the single album The Calling.","title":"Huh Ji-won","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huh_Ji-won"}},"Q61100680":{"id":"Q61100680","name":"Kim Woo-jin","ko":"김우진","birthName":"김우진","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Woojin"],"birth":"1997-04-08","death":"","birthplace":"Bucheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2017","agencies":[{"name":"JYP Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483238","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q46134670","name":"Stray Kids","start":"2017","end":"2019"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/woooojin0408/","x":"https://x.com/woooojinn","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCdhdg9ISE9OYvL8uR9gIzNw","tiktok":"https://www.tiktok.com/@woooojin","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/8d6251d3-d479-4e8f-a17e-4fa8e86d240f"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kim Woojin is a South Korean singer and actor. He is a former member of the boy group Stray Kids, formed by JYP Entertainment in 2017. After leaving the group in late 2019, Kim debuted as a soloist in 2021 with the release of his first extended play (EP) The Moment: A Minor. Kim has since released two additional EPs. Outside of music, Kim has ventured into acting, most notably with a starring role in HBO Max's Brazilian TV series Além do Guarda-Roupa (English: My Magic Closet). Originally signed to 10x Entertainment for solo activities, Kim has been under contract to Kustomade since the label's acquisition by SM Entertainment in 2024.","title":"Kim Woojin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Woojin"}},"Q6409608":{"id":"Q6409608","name":"Kim Yeon-woo","ko":"김연우","birthName":"김학철","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kim Hak-chul"],"birth":"1971-07-22","death":"","birthplace":"Samcheok","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"1995","agencies":[{"name":"Stone Music Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483971","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q7830499","name":"Toy","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/72d9aed3-c30f-4e42-9744-f9d62a5f4e81"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kim Hak-chul, better known by his stage name Kim Yeon-woo is a South Korean male singer, vocal coach, and professor at Seoul Arts College. Nicknamed God of Vocals, he is well known for his ballads, smooth singing voice, and ability to hit high notes without difficulty. Kim recorded a number of hit ballads with the South Korean band, Toy, in the mid-to-late 1990s, gathering a sizable cult following. In 2011, Kim achieved widespread fame and recognition in South Korea through his participation on I Am a Singer, along with numerous appearances on variety and entertainment shows.","title":"Kim Yeon-woo","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Yeon-woo"}},"Q64177288":{"id":"Q64177288","name":"Kang Min-ju","ko":"강민주","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Minju","Kang Minju"],"birth":"2001-03-11","death":"","birthplace":"Masan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q55715778","name":"GWSN","start":"","end":""}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q65054024":{"id":"Q65054024","name":"Kim Min-seok","ko":"김민석","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Laun"],"birth":"1999-08-12","death":"","birthplace":"","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q35101861","name":"ONF","start":"","end":""}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q67981192":{"id":"Q67981192","name":"Kogyeol","ko":"고결","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Go Minsoo"],"birth":"1996-05-19","death":"","birthplace":"","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q21012399","name":"Up10tion","start":"","end":""}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q73799496":{"id":"Q73799496","name":"Park Yu-rim","ko":"박유림","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Yurim"],"birth":"1998-04-13","death":"","birthplace":"South Korea","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singe